# Start-of-work gate: plan + branch

Before editing code for **any new bugfix or feature**, first check whether we
are **already in the midst of one**:

- **Already in progress** (proceed, no challenge) when EITHER:
  - the current git branch matches `phase-*` (a dedicated feature/fix branch), OR
  - an active plan exists for this work (a `.cursor/plans/*.mdc`, or a plan just
    approved this session).
- **Not in progress** (challenge required): the branch is `main` (or another
  base branch) and there is no active plan for the requested work.

## The challenge

When not already in progress, **STOP before making edits** and propose both:

1. A plan file at `.cursor/plans/<YYYY-MM>-<slug>.mdc` (skip a full plan only for
   truly trivial one-liners such as a typo or comment — when unsure, write it).
2. A phase branch `phase-N-<slug>` created from an updated `main`
   (`git switch main && git pull`, then `git switch -c phase-N-<slug>`).

Wait for the user to confirm (or adjust) before editing. Do not commit directly
to `main`.

## After approval

Follow [development-rules.mdc](development-rules.mdc) for the full phase git and
"finish up" workflow (commit → merge to `main` ff-only → push → archive the plan
to `.cursor/plans/executed/` → delete the phase branch → `npm run deploy:prod`),
and give a QA checklist at the end of each phase.
